AI-Powered OSINT Intelligence Platform on HPC Cluster
Project Overview:

This project presents a distributed, AI-powered OSINT platform built on an HPC cluster to collect,
process, and analyze open-source intelligence data for cybersecurity threat detection.

Objectives:
- Build scalable OSINT system
- Use HPC (MPI + SLURM)
- Apply AI for threat detection
- Integrate IDS logs
- Provide monitoring dashboard

Core Modules:
1. OSINT Data Collection
2. HPC Parallel Processing
3. AI Engine
4. Security Intelligence
5. Monitoring Dashboard
6. Cloud Integration
7. Traffic Management

Advanced Features:
- Threat Intelligence Correlation
- Explainable AI
- Attack Graph Visualization
- Real-time Streaming
- Automated Response (SOAR)
- Attack Simulation
- HPC Benchmarking
- Zero Trust Security

Demo Flow:
1. Collect data2. Process via HPC
3. AI detects threat
4. Generate alert
5. Display dashboard

Conclusion:
This project demonstrates integration of AI, HPC, OSINT, and security into a real-world cyber Intelligence Platform 
